From 075921bfa65c0d20c93f177daf863872468bc011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:15:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(contour): user-set start point on closed 2D contours

An optional links.approach.start_point starts the nearest closed
contour ring at the pick's projection onto the cutter-centre path, on
every level, with the lead-in planned there. Refused by name, never
moved silently: a pick far from every ring, no lead-in fitting at the
pick, tabs, control/wear compensation, open chains, tilted contours and
every other operation kind. No pick keeps every path byte-identical.
Saved in the project file only when set; the MCP edit_operation patch
reaches it.

Refs #1448

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
